==Trivia==
*Goblins are small, grotesque, monstrous creatures that appear in the folklore of multiple European cultures. First attested in stories from the Middle Ages, they are ascribed conflicting abilities, temperaments, and appearances depending on the story and country of origin, ranging from mischievous household spirits to malicious, bestial thieves. They often have magical abilities similar to a fairy or demon, such as the ability to shapeshift. Similar creatures include [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duende duendes], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kobold kobolds], [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leprechaun leprechauns], and [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghoul ghouls].
**In the German and Dutch language setting of the game, the Spear Goblins' name translates to "Spear Kobolds". In the Spanish, Arabic, and Vietnamese language setting of the game, the Spear Goblins' name translates to "Duendes with Spears", "Spear Ghouls", and "Spear Throwing Leprechauns" respectively.
**The Spear Goblins are 1 of 17 [[cards]] associated with [[Goblins]], with the others being [[Goblin Gang]], [[Baby Goblins]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Goblin Demolisher]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Goblin Barrel]], [[Goblin Curse]], [[Goblin Drill]], [[Goblin Machine]], [[Party Rocket]], [[Party Hut]], [[Goblinstein]], and of course, Goblins.
***The Goblins, Spear Goblins, Goblin Cage, and Goblin Hut are the only cards associated with Goblins that are unlocked in Goblin Stadium.
*Spear throwing is believed to have been in use by Homo Sapiens since the Upper Paleolithic, at around 30,000 years ago. Most stratified European finds come from the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magdalenian Magdalenian]. In this period, elaborate pieces, often in the form of animals, are common. The earliest reliable data concerning atlatls have come from several caves in France dating to the Upper Paleolithic, about 21,000 to 17,000 years ago. The earliest known example is a 17,500-year-old Solutrean atlatl made of reindeer antler, found at Combe Saunière (Dordogne), France. Spear throwing was later supplemented by the bow and arrow in the Epi-Paleolithic, until it was added to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancient_Olympic_Games Ancient Olympic Games] as part of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pentathlon pentathlon] in 708 BC.
**The Spear Goblins' spears can be seen on the [[Trophies|Trophy Road]] as a decoration.
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Gary and uses an spear-related card in their [[Battle Decks|deck]] which is Spear Goblins. This is a reference to the name origin of the name "Gary", which means "''spear king''".
*The Spear Goblins are 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
*The Spear Goblins are one of the first troop cards to be featured in a Trainer's deck, alongside the [[Minions]], [[Archers]], [[Knight]], Goblins, Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Minion Horde, [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Hog Rider]], Baby Dragon, [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], and [[Balloon]].
*The Spear Goblins are 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Stun Attack|Stun Attack]] [[buff]], the others being Witch and [[Executioner]].
*Their [[Star Points|Star Level 3 Skin]] grants them a red mohawk similar to the Level 6 Goblin in Clash of Clans.
*Out of all [[Emotes]] with Goblins as a subject, 1 Emote has a Goblin wearing a bandana, and can be safely assumed to be a Spear Goblin.
*The Spear Goblins were featured in the winning decks of multiple Clash Royale Tournaments. More specifically:
**The Spear Goblins were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VxEzjdKQ4HA Clash Royale Helsinki Tournament], by a player called Jason.
**The Spear Goblins were featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/h3IOFTfT8Sk?si=wTF1FekCifpSULn- Clash Royale League 2020 Tournament], by a player called Ruben.
*On 1/4/2019, a Clash Royale [https://x.com/ClashRoyale/status/1112701338012532737 tweet] on Twitter showcased a fake Spear Goblins balance change. The Spear Gobins would gain a 4th Spear Goblin that would be able to deal Area Damage. However, it never made it into the game.

